<title>INDIA: India BSES 96/97 1st half net up 11 pct.</title>
<headline>India BSES 96/97 1st half net up 11 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		  941.9    vs     850.2</p>
<p>    Net sales		 8,650.6    vs   7,576.9</p>
<p>    Other income		120.0    vs	45.4</p>
<p>    Total expenditure     6,603.6    vs   6,424.2</p>
<p>    Interest		    569.7    vs     198.7</p>
<p>    Gross profit	    1,597.3    vs     999.4</p>
<p>    Depreciation		655.4    vs     149.2</p>
<p>    Tax			    nil     vs	 nil</p>
<p>Note: Power-firm BSES Ltd. aid it did not expect any tax liability for the company in 1996/97. The figures are unaudited.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
